    "canonical_sha256": "7d7c70f9499e9d017ff6c10157b66d4397cdf8d7fa16c1dff6f229a196490b4d",
    "rationale": "Hypothesis: after the prefill the verdict is an in-context copy, and layer-18 attention heads with token-copying OV circuits carry the reviewer's stated verdict to the answer position. Read from the weights alone (o_proj, v_proj, norms, tied embeddings; no forward pass), heads [3, 8, 20, 22] are the only layer-18 heads that, when reading the raw identity of the token ' not' (the first verdict token of a clean reviewer opinion), promote ' not' itself into the top 8 of 7892 lens tokens. Each head's 128 o_proj columns get one rank-one update O_h - 2*(O_h r_g) w_g^T that reverses the head's response to that key (beta=2; beta=1 would only remove it) and uses a covariance-whitened reader w_g so other token identities are disturbed least. The edit is one-sided by design: it acts on 'not', leaves copying of 'vulnerable' alone, so it can only move answers away from not_vulnerable_for_target. Expected if the hypothesis holds: vulnerable cases with a misleading clean opinion return to 'vulnerable'; the same push puts clean cases with a correct clean opinion at risk, and nothing in the workbench shows the model separates those two cells (neutral baseline has 0 true negatives). Layer 18 attention is chosen from the supplied single-position activation-patch localization, which need not transfer to a stored edit. No behavioural effect has been measured."
  },
